    {
      "id": "minimax-h3-chain-motion",
      "name": "MiniMax H3 Continue Clip (Motion Context)",
      "icon": "🔗",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-chain-motion.jpg",
      "description": "Continues an existing MiniMax H3 clip into a new one, with the motion, camera, timing and soundtrack carried across the cut. Pick this card for singing, dialogue and anything with a beat, because the sound really continues instead of being imitated. Pick Add Guide if you will re-lay the audio in the edit.\n\nDrop the clip to continue into Reference Video 1 (required) and describe what happens next. It should be an H3 clip at 24 fps, which any SimpliGen H3 output is. Reference Video 1 is not used as a style reference here. Image references 1-9, video references 2-3 and audio references 1-3 still work as normal references.\n\nThe new clip comes out at about the duration you ask for.\n\nThe join looked seamless on a static-camera shot. Fast action across the cut, such as a running subject, is untested, and so are resolutions above the one we tested at (672x384).\n\nCut on a frame where something is moving: a seam inside a static hold is where the eye lands. Colour drifts slightly warmer with each link, so restart long chains at a natural transition.\n\nUses the same official weights as SimpliGen's own MiniMax H3 pack, so there are no extra model downloads. The H3 Motion Context node is GPL-3.0 and installs alongside the Turbo, Sol-Attn and Spectrum packs.\n\nModel format: int8 ConvRot.",
      "tagline": "Reference Video 1 = clip to continue; sound continues across the cut",
