      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-director-two-shot.jpg",
      "description": "Makes two connected shots in one render, so you get a single file with the join already made and no clip to feed back in. It uses AIMixer's MiniMax H3 Director.\n\nWrite the prompt the way H3 wants it: [Shot 1] ... then [Shot 2] ... Everything before [Shot 2] is the first shot and everything after it is the second. An \"At 00:05.000,\" stamp after the tag is removed. With no [Shot 2] in the prompt, both shots run the same prompt, continued.\n\nEach shot is as long as the Duration slider, so 5 s gives a 10 s clip. A 10 s clip at 672x384 takes about 7 minutes on a 12 GB card.\n\nReferences 1-9, video references and audio references go to both shots. The dialogue field is added to the end of the prompt, so it lands in the second shot when a [Shot 2] exists. To give each shot its own speech, write it inline with <d> tags instead.\n\nThe join holds well, with almost no colour shift and steady audio across it. This card is fixed at two shots.\n\nModel format: int8 ConvRot.",
